WEBVTT

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.380
Right then, Alto Goldfield.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.080
Would you like to join the Executive Committee
of the Student Council?

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.460
You want ME to join the Council?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.830
Yes. I presume it's something
you'd be interested in as well.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.500
Is it just so you can keep a closer eye on me?

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.540
If that's how you'd like to see it, sure.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.580
You ARE harboring a demon
within the walls of our academy.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.630
But I truly do want you on our Council.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:47.210
You dueled Chris, one of the top five
most powerful mages at this institution.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:52.750
Your familiar may be a demon,
but even so, she is a formidable opponent.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.500
Then there's this most recent incident.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.420
Where Chris got hurt...

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.290
We still don't know what motivates the perpetrators.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.580
If you assert that your familiar acts with no ill intentions,

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.460
then would you not be interested
in using your powers to protect the Academy?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.580
Black or white? Tangled up, they turn gray

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.880
Everything always seems so ambiguous

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:54.790
I walk by your side as you smile, helpless

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.170
Admiration clear as day

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:01.460
Shining out across the endless distance

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:07.210
Cast a spell on this pitiful situation with an Abracada-Boo

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:13.420
There's a loneliness hidden beneath the darkness in your eyes

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:20.170
I wish I could embrace it with a gentle song

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.710
Even the whole world starts to shout it's all a lie,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.670
As long as you are as you are

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:33.880
I'll sweep through with a glimmering wind and scream out the truth

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.460
Even if the whole world yells out that it's a sin,

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.250
Even if I'm all on my own

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.330
I want to keep learning to understand you

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:48.830
I'm on your side, I'll protect you

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.790
<b>SELECTION</b>

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.580
You're joining the Student Council?!

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:00.420
Yeah.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.790
Why? How?! What happened for them to invite you on?!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.460
I-I'm not entirely sure myself,
but the President herself wants me there.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.380
I can't tell them what the REAL reason is…

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.380
Please tell everyone we saw you had potential
and invited you to join.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:30.290
Well, you did beat Chris in a duel.
With that in mind, it only seems natural you'd be invited.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.080
We've NEVER had a second-year student
on the council before, either!

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.630
R-really?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.630
Really! You should be proud of yourself!

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:48.210
Well, this came out of the blue.
I was worried for a bit, there, but…

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.920
Hey, I'm happy for you!

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:51.920
Huh?

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.420
You've always wanted to move up.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.960
You're incredible, Alto.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.880
Th-thanks.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.080
All right! I won't let you get too far ahead of me!

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:11.380
I'm gonna make sure I get a better score than you
on the Bronze exam!

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.420
Why the long face?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:20.540
Huh?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:27.250
Oh, I just… People ended up finding out what you are,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.080
and I feel like the Student Council
forced us into this new position…

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.250
Eh, even if they're spying on you,
they won't be on you twenty-four seven.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.290
And I don't care that they know what I am.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.500
But I want you to be careful around the Council.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:50.040
That girl gives me a bad vibe…
like she's not really human.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:55.920
You mean the President? I mean, she was kinda scary…

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.540
Remember how I shook my head
when she repeated her question?

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.500
You were in real danger then.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:05.290
Same with that last invitation.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:12.080
If you'd turned her down,
she might've taken off your head.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.460
O-oh, come on! She wouldn't have gone that far!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.920
True, maybe taking off your head's a stretch.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.080
But she's definitely not normal.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:31.290
Still, the President aside, yesterday was an eye-opener.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:37.040
If I'd been stronger,
I might've been able to protect you better.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.790
I might've kept your identity a secret, too.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:45.790
If things like that keep happening, eventually,
we won't be able to lie to everyone anymore.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.790
And if that happens, then you'll be in danger.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.580
I want to get stronger.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.670
Strong enough to keep you safe.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:02.380
D-don't get the wrong idea! I didn't mean that
in a weird way! I just…

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.380
Why not? That doesn't bother me.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.330
Huh? But, Vermeil…

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.290
I was really happy to hear it.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.830
In that case, though, I'm going to have
to help you get much stronger.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.040
Huh?

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.540
Whoa, hey!

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.460
What're you...?

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.080
I can't hear you.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.330
You want to keep me safe, right?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.040
W-well yeah, but… this has nothing to do with that!

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.880
Quiet, you! No one who lets me win can keep me safe!

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:57.750
I gotta... I gotta get stronger!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.500
Vermeil is a demon.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:13.830
Finally… at long last, I've found it.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:19.790
Vermeil might be a demon, but she's not a BAD demon!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.920
The world's greatest scourge, is she?

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:51.790
That's right. I'm gonna get even stronger than I am now.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.380
So no matter what happens, I can keep Vermeil safe.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.170
Vermeil, just you watch.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.630
I'll be stronger than the Council members one day.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:09.420
No, I'll be the strongest person in the entire world!

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:18.330
Setting aside how I got there,
I'm on the Student Council now.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.540
I'll learn everything I can from them.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:26.330
I'll work hard so one day,
I can say with pride that I'm Vermeil's master!

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.000
Pardon me!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.290
Oh.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:55.960
Huh?

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:05.880
ALTOOOO GOOOOOLDFIELD!

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.420
Madame President!

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:14.540
I must object to having this shameless boy
join our illustrious Council!

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:20.630
We made a mistake in forgetting to lock the door.
This situation isn't his fault.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.750
You mustn't be so lax, Madame President!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.830
This is hardly reason for reprimand,
nor reason to be distressed.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:27.790
What?!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.380
A…

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.420
A man has seen our nearly-naked figures
before our wedding days!

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:39.710
Goodness, Jessica. You're more demure
and traditional than I expected.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:46.710
Huh?! Am... am I the weird one here?! I can't be!

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.130
Moving right along…

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.380
Let me present you with the reason
I've gathered you all here today.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.130
I want you all to examine this.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:55.880
What is it?

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.710
A magical element used by the mage I fought.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:03.960
However, it's only one part of a much larger whole.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.170
I've never seen this kind of magic before.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:16.420
You said it was a simple paper golem, yes?

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.540
Still, though…

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.500
From the investigation performed
by the Ortigia Police's appraisal specialists,

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:28.880
this form of magic matched nothing recorded
before in the Bank of Magicks.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:31.250
An unrecorded form of magic…

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.790
Within that single piece of paper lies
a magic formula more complex than fathomable.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:43.130
Not even the Gold Square
appraisal specialists could decipher it.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.130
Then that means…

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.460
No…

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:56.750
"Those who plunge into the abyss of knowledge
and craft new forms of magic..."

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:03.290
"Those whose discoveries revolutionize our world..."

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:08.080
"Unto those few do we bequeath a title
deserving of the nation's utmost respect:"

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.830
Our enemy may be a Platinum Square.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:26.630
This sucks!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.000
I'm exhausted!

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.920
Huh? Hey, it's Kohakumiya!

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.750
<b>PLATINUM</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.750
<b>SQUARE</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.750
<b>KOHAKUMIYA</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.750
<b>"OF THE WAVES"</b>

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.330
Hello, Iolite.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:50.580
Did you get the stuff I got for you?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.040
Could you get a move on? It was a real chore, y'know.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.170
That's besides the point, Iolite.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:01.330
You've again broken the paper doll I gave you
to communicate with me, haven't you?

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:07.670
Man, I always forget how huge you are!
Glad I made the trip out.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.290
Are you listening?

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.040
At any rate, you took a while.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:31.420
It was such a pain! That old high priest
was so stubborn! He just wouldn't give in!

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.250
He didn't have to be so annoying!

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.210
The high priest…

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.880
You mean Haesval of the Gilded Tower?

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:45.710
He's the most skilled caster of divine magic
amongst the Platinum Squares!

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.580
However did you get him to agree?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.420
I killed him.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.580
How else?

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:06.880
Meh, it is what it is!
Good luck with those demon parts, now!

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.290
What's next?

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.960
First, I gotta change. Then we can head out again.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:16.960
After all,

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:23.670
we gotta go pick up the bits
that SOMEONE forgot to take with them.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:32.830
I'm such a busy little bee!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.880
What is this place?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:47.290
A girl is crying. Who is she?

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:51.460
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.710
I know. She's…

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.630
Huh? Where…?

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:07.540
Hello.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.920
What do you feel for her?

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:18.380
Huh? Who's 'her'?

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:21.790
A woman? Who is she?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.830
There are two paths before you.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:35.670
One is righteous and serves to benefit
all of mankind, the path of justice.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:44.420
One is selfish and serves to benefit her
and only her, the path of destruction.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:50.380
Oh, I understand.
The girl she's speaking about must be…

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:55.630
What…

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:00.080
…do you feel for her?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.170
What was that?

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.540
Goodness, you're still at it?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.540
Vermeil!

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:37.790
You've been doing this every night.
Tonight, you should try to sleep early, all right?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:44.460
I-I know, but the Bronze exam
is almost here, and I'm nervous.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:51.580
True, but half the student body will pass this exam, yes?
That's a piece of cake for you.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:59.460
I'd be more confident if it were just a written exam,
but there's a practical part, too.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:03.500
And the Council members
are pressuring me to do well, too...

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:08.580
The incident is important,
but you should focus on your Bronze exam.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.790
It's about that time, huh?

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:19.500
Second-year Alto, surely you wouldn't fail
your exam after beating me, yes?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.380
So I've gotta pass, no matter what…

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.960
You're naked! Put some clothes on!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:39.420
If you're worried about the practical exam,
then you shouldn't be stuck at your desk.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:41.710
Hey!

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.710
You're gonna use me for the exam, right?

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.710
Then I'm gonna need lots of mana.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.210
But…

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.460
She's draining me…

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.830
C'mon, now you.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.130
You were going to stay up late anyways, weren't you?

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.790
I'll suck it out of you, and you suck it out of me.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:20.580
Let's get that practice in, all right?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:28.670
All right, I have my pen, I have my notebook…

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:31.290
And some textbooks, too, just in case…

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:40.250
This is... the book Vermeil was sealed in.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:47.460
Feels like so long ago that I couldn't summon
a familiar and was about to repeat the grade…

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.130
Nope, still can't read it.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:59.880
Oh, yeah, a mage sealed her in that book, right?
I wonder who they were...

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:08.170
Alto, don't you have to get going soon?

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.750
Huh? It's already this late?!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:30.000
It's finally time for the Bronze exam!
Let's give it our best shot!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.710
Yay!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.670
Y-yeah.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.330
Hey! Liven up, now!

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.830
S-sorry, I didn't sleep well…

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:43.040
I swear! Taking care of yourself
is an important skill, so get it together!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.750
R-right.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:53.790
I've got lots of mana now, and my heart's working fine.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:58.500
Maybe I was right to take Vermeil up on her advice.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:04.130
We're in Building A, right?

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.580
We should be.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.580
It would've been so much easier
if they'd just let us take it at the Academy…

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.210
Apprentice mages from all over the nation
will be coming to take the Bronze exam!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:18.170
They picked a neutral place
so no one has an advantage!

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:20.000
Hey, look at them.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.290
Those uniforms are Ortigia.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:22.000
Oh, them.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.460
They're from Ortigia.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.040
Why do I feel like we stand out?

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.420
Our school is extremely competitive.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:36.830
50 percent of our students pass,
but at other schools, only 10 percent may pass.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:42.130
Ortigia is also the only school
that requires Bronze to advance to Fourth Year.

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:48.170
Wow. That makes the Bronze exam
feel like a way bigger deal.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.540
Y-yeah.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:53.540
And with that in mind, Marx…
I'm surprised you got in here.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:57.920
But of course I did, because I have a secret weapon!

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.290
Well, in either case,
don't go getting careless on the exam!

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.170
All right! I'm pumped!

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.000
And we're starting off with the practical exam…

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:13.250
A-all right! I'm gonna pass!

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.210
That's the spirit!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:27.040
There's a lot of people here, and I heard
this is only one of ten sites for the practical.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:27.830
Yeah.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:31.210
But what's everyone murmuring about?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.630
There's something inside that crystal… a flame?

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.330
All right, everyone here?

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:51.420
I'm only going to explain this once, so listen up!

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:53.330
It's him!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.250
You know him, Cheryl?

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:58.330
That's Colonel Pharanx of the Royal Mage Corps.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:02.380
He's the "demonic" mage
specially selected for Special Ops.

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:05.880
I can't believe he's our proctor…

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:15.080
This year's practical exercise is all about mana provision!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:21.330
This giant crystal can measure the amount
and quality of your mana!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.830
But don't think it's just a boring old measurement device!

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:28.830
We're testing your ability to supply mana
to an entity through a physical barrier

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:31.580
by having you supply mana through the crystal
to this amorphous flame!

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.880
As such, you'll pour as much mana as you can
into the contained flame!

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:39.880
The amount you're able to provide
will determine your score!

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.540
Wh-what?

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.170
That sounds kinda easy.

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:47.540
So we just need to fill the crystal with mana, right?

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.330
All right, let's start with Student #1!

00:21:55.290 --> 00:22:01.750
No... there's no way this is going to be THAT easy.

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:22.580
Does it get easier with time for the immortal?

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:33.290
If I was born normal, if I become normal, can I stay close?

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:38.710
With the children, we link our arms

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:43.920
Make a circle and sing a song

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:50.670
Knowing there was no chair for me all along

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:55.960
You locked me into the dark, I'm your preserved flower

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:59.630
The world is too slow to understand

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:03.210
Not all blossoms spark, And spikes may be sharp

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:07.750
They only want to see the beautiful parts

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:11.130
Sitting in a shower of scarlet rain

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:15.460
It all used to be ours, I'm counting the hours

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.920
Hours that stood between us like a river

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:20.920
Once I crawled through the water

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:26.460
All I ever knew have become distant past
